<title>MEXICO: Mexico's TMM launches new $20 mln ship.</title>
<headline>Mexico's TMM launches new $20 mln ship.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican transportation company Transportacion Maritima Mexicana (TMM) launched a new $20 million ship called &quot;Marques de Comillas&quot; for its Spain-Canary Islands route, TMM said on Monday.</p>
<p>In a statement from Vigo, Spain, TMM said the ship was built through its Spanish affiliate Compania Transatlantica Espanola, which TMM acquired in April.</p>
<p>TMM said the new ship &quot;will reinforce the route between Spain and the Canary Islands.&quot;</p>
<p>The company is the largest shipper in Latin America, and has been focusing on improving its European and Asian operations.</p>
<p>((-- Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
